{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000858877-26-000156", "published_at": "2026-10-09T20:08:49Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-09T20:08:49Z", "headline": "Cisco: Director or officer departure or appointment", "body": "false000085887700008588772026-10-072026-10-07 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ___________________________________ FORM 8-K ___________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): October 7, 2026 ___________________________________ CISCO SYSTEMS, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) ___________________________________ ___________________________________ Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions (see General Instruction A.2. below): Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (§ 230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (§ 240.12b-2 of this chapter).", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["CSCO"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/858877/000085887726000156/0000858877-26-000156-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000731766-26-000255", "published_at": "2026-10-13T10:14:45Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T10:14:45Z", "headline": "UnitedHealth Group: Results of operations and financial condition", "body": "Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On October 13, 2026, UnitedHealth Group Incorporated (the “Company”) issued a press release announcing its third quarter 2026 results. A copy of the press release is furnished herewith as Exhibit 99.1. The press release also includes a hyperlink to a pdf document which is furnished herewith as Exhibit 99.2. Exhibits 99.1 and 99.2 are incorporated herein by reference. The information in this", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["UNH"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/731766/000073176626000255/0000731766-26-000255-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001628280-26-065582", "published_at": "2026-10-13T10:30:38Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T10:30:38Z", "headline": "JPMorgan Chase & Co. Earnings Release - Third Quarter 2026 Results", "body": "EX-99.1 2 a3q26erfexhibit991narrative.htm JPMORGAN CHASE & CO. EARNINGS RELEASE - THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS Exhibit 99.1 JPMORGANCHASE REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2026 NET INCOME OF $15.3 BILLION ($5.57 PER SHARE), NET INCOME OF $15.8 BILLION ($5.75 PER SHARE) EXCLUDING A SIGNIFICANT ITEM THIRD-QUARTER 2026 RESULTS 1 SIGNIFICANT ITEM IN 3Q26 RESULTS n $658 million of net investment securities losses in Corporate10 ($0.18 decrease in EPS11) CAPITAL DISTRIBUTIONS n Common dividend of $4.4 billion or $1.65 per share n $664 million of common stock net repurchases12 n Net payout LTM12,13 of 61% FORTRESS PRINCIPLES n Book value per share of $132.30, up 6% YoY; tangible book value per share2 of $112.64, up 7% YoY n Basel III common equity Tier 1 capital3 of $304 billion, Standardized ratio3 of 13.9% and Advanced ratio3 of 14.1% n Firm supplementary leverage ratio of 5.5% SUPPORTED CONSUMERS, BUSINESSES & COMMUNITIES n Approximately $2.9 trillion of credit and capital14 raised YTD: n $240 billion of credit for consumers n $27 billion of credit for U.S. small businesses n $2.5 trillion of credit and capital for corporations15 and non-U.S.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["JPM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026065582/0001628280-26-065582-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001067491-26-000040", "published_at": "2026-10-13T11:25:54Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T11:25:54Z", "headline": "Infosys: Company Statement On The U.s. Permanent Labor Certification Program", "body": "6-K 1 index.htm INDEX UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 Form 6-K Report of Foreign Private Issuer Pursuant to Rule 13a-16 or 15d-16 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 For the month of October 2026 Commission File Number 001-35754 Infosys Limited (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) Not Applicable. (Translation of Registrant's name into English) Electronics City, Hosur Road, Bengaluru - 560 100, Karnataka, India. +91-80-2852-0261 (Address of principal executive offices) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant files or will file annual reports under cover Form 20-F or Form 40-F: Form 20-F þ Form 40-F o Indicate by check mark if the registrant is submitting the Form 6-K in paper as permitted by Regulation S-T Rule 101(b)(1): o Indicate by check mark if the registrant is submitting the Form 6-K in paper as permitted by Regulation S-T Rule 101(b)(7): o TABLE OF CONTENTS COMPANY STATEMENT ON THE U.S.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["INFY"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1067491/000106749126000040/0001067491-26-000040-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000886982-26-000529", "published_at": "2026-10-13T11:32:56Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T11:32:56Z", "headline": "Goldman Sachs: Third Quarter 2026 Earnings Results", "body": "1 THIRD QUARTER 2026 EARNINGS RESULTS Goldman Sachs Reports Third Quarter Earnings Per Common Share of $17.01 Financial Summary NEW YORK, October 13, 2026 – The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. (NYSE: GS) today reported net revenues of $18.68 billion and net earnings of $5.29 billion for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026. Net revenues were $56.24 billion and net earnings were $17.55 billion for the first nine months of 2026. Diluted earnings per common share (EPS)1 was $17.01 for the third quarter of 2026 compared with $12.25 for the third quarter of 2025 and $20.98 for the second quarter of 2026, and was $55.56 for the first nine months of 2026 compared with $37.33 for the first nine months of 2025. Annualized return on average common shareholders' equity (ROE)2 was 18.7% for the third quarter of 2026 and 20.7% for the first nine months of 2026. Book value per common share increased by 1.4% during the third quarter of 2026 and by 4.2% during the first nine months of 2026 to $372.64.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["GS"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000088698226000529/0000886982-26-000529-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000200406-26-000189", "published_at": "2026-10-13T12:12:35Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T12:12:35Z", "headline": "Johnson & Johnson reports Q3 2026 results, raises 2026 guidance", "body": "•2026 Third-Quarter reported sales growth of 5.9% to $25.4 Billion with operational growth of 6.0%* and adjusted operational growth of 6.1%* •2026 Third-Quarter earnings per share (EPS) of $0.09 reflects a one-time special charge for the proposed talc litigation resolution, the acquisition of Firefly Bio, Inc., and the strategic collaboration with Sail Biomedicines; adjusted EPS* of $2.59 also reflects the impact of these M&A deals •Strong operational performance results in the Company increasing 2026 guidance with estimated reported sales of $101.2 Billion or 7.4% at the midpoint and increasing adjusted EPS* guidance by $0.06 to $11.10 or 2.9% at the midpoint •Significant innovation including the market authorization of OTTAVA as the world’s first table-integrated soft tissue robotic system, approval of IMAAVY in warm autoimmune hemolytic anemia (wAIHA), and priority review for RYBREVANT FASPRO for advanced head and neck cancer New Brunswick, N.J. (October 13, 2026) – Johnson & Johnson (NYSE: JNJ) today announced results for third-quarter 2026.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["JNJ"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/200406/000020040626000189/0000200406-26-000189-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001628280-26-065616", "published_at": "2026-10-13T13:38:53Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T13:38:53Z", "headline": "JPMorgan Chase & Co. Earnings Presentation Slides - Financial Results - 3Q26", "body": "EX-99 2 a3q26_earningsxpresentat.htm JPMORGAN CHASE & CO. EARNINGS PRESENTATION SLIDES - FINANCIAL RESULTS - 3Q26 October 13, 2026 3Q26 Financial Results Exhibit 99 3Q26 Financial highlights ROTCE1 20% CET1 capital ratios2 Std. 13.9% | Adv. 14.1% Total Loss-Absorbing Capacity2 $599B Std. RWA3 $2.2T Cash and marketable securities4 $1.5T Average loans $1.6T 1 See note 3 on slide 9 2 Represents the estimated Basel III common equity Tier 1 (“CET1”) capital and ratio and Total Loss-Absorbing Capacity for the current period 3 Standardized risk-weighted assets (“RWA”). Estimated for the current period 4 Cash and marketable securities represent HQLA and unencumbered marketable securities. Estimated for the current period. See note 1 on slide 10 5 See note 5 on slide 9 6 See note 1 on slide 9 7 Includes the net impact of employee issuances.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["JPM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026065616/0001628280-26-065616-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000080424-26-000214", "published_at": "2026-10-13T14:01:56Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T14:01:56Z", "headline": "Procter & Gamble: P&G Declares Quarterly Dividend", "body": "P&G Shareholders Also Elect All 12 P&G Director Nominees at 2026 Annual Meeting CINCINNATI, October 13, 2026 – The Procter & Gamble Company (NYSE:PG) announced at today’s Annual Meeting of Shareholders that the P&G Board of Directors declared a quarterly dividend of $1.0885 per share on the Common Stock and on the Series A and Series B ESOP Convertible Class A Preferred Stock of the Company, payable on or after November 16, 2026 to Common Stock shareholders of record at the close of business on October 23, 2026, and to Series A and Series B ESOP Convertible Class A Preferred Stock shareholders of record at the start of business on October 23, 2026. P&G has been paying a dividend for 136 consecutive years since its incorporation in 1890 and has increased its dividend for 70 consecutive years. This reinforces our commitment to return cash to shareowners, many of whom rely on the steady, reliable income earned with their investment in P&G. Also at today’s Annual Meeting, P&G shareholders elected all 12 P&G Director nominees, with each receiving strong support according to preliminary voting results.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["PG"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/80424/000008042426000214/0000080424-26-000214-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000310158-26-000237", "published_at": "2026-10-13T16:36:57Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-13T16:36:57Z", "headline": "Paul J. Diaz Elected to Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, N.J., USA Board of Directors", "body": "RAHWAY, N.J., Oct. 13, 2026 – Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, N.J., USA (NYSE: MRK), known as MSD outside the United States and Canada, today announced that Paul J. Diaz, managing partner at Cressey & Company, will join the Company’s Board of Directors effective Nov. 1, 2026. He will stand for election by the company’s shareholders in May 2027. With the addition of Mr. Diaz, the Merck board will consist of 14 members. “We are pleased to welcome Paul Diaz to our Board. Paul brings extensive leadership and business expertise in the healthcare industry, and we look forward to his contributions and insights,” said Rob Davis, chairman and chief executive officer. Mr. Diaz is a managing partner at Cressey & Company, a private investment firm focused on investing in and cultivating high-quality health care firms. He previously served as president and chief executive officer of Myriad Genetics, Inc., a leading genetic testing and precision medicine company. Before that, he served as president and chief executive officer of Kindred Healthcare, a Fortune 500 healthcare services company. Mr.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["MRK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/310158/000031015826000237/0000310158-26-000237-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-420933", "published_at": "2026-10-14T10:02:14Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T10:02:14Z", "headline": "HDFC Bank: Secretarial & Group Oversight", "body": null, "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["HDFCBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1144967/000119312526420933/0001193125-26-420933-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000070858-26-000481", "published_at": "2026-10-14T10:44:44Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T10:44:44Z", "headline": "Bank of America: Results of operations and financial condition; Regulation FD disclosure", "body": "RESULTS OF OPERATIONS AND FINANCIAL CONDITION. On October 14, 2026, Bank of America Corporation (the “Corporation”) announced financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026, reporting third quarter net income of $6.9 billion, or $0.91 per diluted share. A copy of the press release announcing the Corporation’s results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026 (the “Press Release”) is attached hereto as Exhibit 99.1 and is incorporated by reference in this", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["BAC"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/70858/000007085826000481/0000070858-26-000481-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000895421-26-000288", "published_at": "2026-10-14T11:39:21Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T11:39:21Z", "headline": "Morgan Stanley Third Quarter 2026 Earnings Results", "body": "Morgan Stanley Reports Net Revenues of $20.3 Billion, EPS of $3.03 and ROTCE of 22.6% NEW YORK, October 14, 2026 – Morgan Stanley (NYSE: MS) today reported net revenues of $20.3 billion for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026 compared with $18.2 billion a year ago. Net income applicable to Morgan Stanley was $4.9 billion, or $3.03 per diluted share, compared with $4.6 billion, or $2.80 per diluted share, for the same period a year ago.1 Highlights •The Firm reported strong net revenues of $20.3 billion and pre-tax income of $6.5 billion demonstrating the continued momentum of our Integrated Firm.4 •The Firm delivered a strong ROTCE of 22.6%.2,6 •The expense efficiency ratio was 66% year to date, demonstrating operating leverage while we continued to invest in our businesses.3,5,12 •The Standardized Common Equity Tier 1 capital ratio was 14.9%.13 •Institutional Securities reported net revenues of $10.0 billion reflecting strong performance in Equity driven by client engagement and strength in Advisory.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["MS"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000288/0000895421-26-000288-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001575872-26-000700", "published_at": "2026-10-14T16:43:28Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T16:43:28Z", "headline": "Dr. Reddy's: report to the SEC (6-K)", "body": "6-K 1 rdy0948_6k.htm FORM 6-K SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 Form 6-K REPORT OF FOREIGN PRIVATE ISSUER PURSUANT TO RULE 13A-16 OR 15D-16 UNDER THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 October, 2026 Commission File Number 1-15182 DR. REDDY’S LABORATORIES LIMITED (Translation of registrant’s name into English) 8-2-337, Road No. 3, Banjara Hills Hyderabad, Telangana 500 034, India +91-40-49002900 (Address of principal executive office) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant files or will file annual reports under cover of Form 20-F or Form 40-F. Form 20-F x Form 40-F ¨ Indicate by check mark if the registrant is submitting the Form 6-K in paper as permitted by Regulation S-T Rule 101(b)(1): ______ Note: Regulation S-T Rule 101(b)(1) only permits the submission in paper of a Form 6-K if submitted solely to provide an attached annual report to security holders.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["DRREDDY"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1135951/000157587226000700/0001575872-26-000700-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000909832-26-000096", "published_at": "2026-10-14T20:16:05Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T20:16:05Z", "headline": "Costco Wholesale Corporation Announces Quarterly Cash Dividend", "body": "EX-99.1 2 costex9918-k101426.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Press Release COSTCO WHOLESALE CORPORATION ANNOUNCES QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND ISSAQUAH, Wash., October 14, 2026 - Costco Wholesale Corporation (“Costco” or the “Company”) (Nasdaq: COST) today announced that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly cash dividend on Costco common stock of $1.47 per share. The quarterly dividend is payable November 13, 2026, to shareholders of record at the close of business on October 30, 2026. Costco currently operates 939 warehouses, including 647 in the United States and Puerto Rico, 115 in Canada, 43 in Mexico, 37 in Japan, 29 in the United Kingdom, 20 in Korea, 15 in Australia, 14 in Taiwan, seven in China, five in Spain, three in France, two in Sweden, and one each in Iceland, and New Zealand. Costco also operates e-commerce sites in the U.S., Canada, the U.K., Mexico, Korea, Taiwan, Japan, Australia, and China. Certain statements contained in this document constitute forward-looking statements within the meaning of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["COST"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/909832/000090983226000096/0000909832-26-000096-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000950103-26-015594", "published_at": "2026-10-14T20:49:49Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-14T20:49:49Z", "headline": "ICICI Bank: Disclosure under Indian Listing Regulations", "body": "IBN ICICI Bank Limited (the Bank) Report on Form 6-K We wish to inform you the following: Call with media on financial results for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026 The Bank will host a conference call with media at 4:00 p.m. (IST) on October 17, 2026, to discuss the financial results of the Bank for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026. Dial-in details to be shared with the participants Earnings call on financial results for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026 The Bank will host an earnings call with analysts and investors at 5:00 p.m. (IST) on October 17, 2026 to discuss the financial results of the Bank for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026. The dial-in details for the conference call are given below: The audio recording and transcript of the above calls will be posted on the Bank's website at https://www.icici.bank.in Please take the above information on record. SIGNATURE Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned, thereunto duly authorised.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["ICICIBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1103838/000095010326015594/0000950103-26-015594-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001104659-26-116198", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:31:00Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-15T19:31:00Z", "headline": "Caterpillar Announces Leadership Transition", "body": "in Resource Industries IRVING, Texas, Oct. 15, 2026 – Caterpillar Inc. today announced Denise Johnson, group president of Resource Industries, has elected to retire effective Feb. 1, 2027. Derrick York, who currently serves as president of Solar Turbines and Caterpillar senior vice president, has been appointed group president of Resource Industries, effective Nov. 1, 2026, at which time Johnson will assume an advisory role to ensure a seamless leadership transition. Since joining Caterpillar in 2011, Johnson has transformed Caterpillar’s mining business and advanced the industry, championing technologies that define the modern mine site. She assumed leadership of Resource Industries in 2016 during a historic mining downturn. Her leadership strengthened operations and the portfolio while maintaining a clear focus on long-term growth, returning the segment to profitability and ultimately delivering its strongest financial performance in more than a decade. “Denise took on a critical role during one of the mining industry’s most challenging times,” said Joe Creed, Caterpillar chairman and CEO.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["CAT"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/18230/000110465926116198/0001104659-26-116198-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001104659-26-116227", "published_at": "2026-10-15T20:00:53Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-15T20:00:53Z", "headline": "AbbVie: Director or officer departure or appointment", "body": "Departure of Directors or Certain Officers; Election of Directors; Appointment of Certain Officers; Compensatory Arrangement of Certain Officers On October 14, 2026, AbbVie Inc. (“AbbVie”) expanded the size of its Board of Directors (the “Board”) from twelve directors to thirteen directors and appointed Dr. John M. Carethers as a Class II director. Dr. Carethers currently serves as the Vice Chancellor for Health Sciences at the University of California San Diego and was previously a director of Avantor, Inc. Dr. Carethers has been appointed to the Public Policy and Sustainability Committee of AbbVie. The Board affirmatively determined that Dr. Carethers is an “independent director” under each of the standards set forth in section 303A.02 of the New York Stock Exchange Listed Company Manual and AbbVie’s Governance Guidelines and Director Independence Guidelines. Dr. Carethers will be entitled to compensation as an independent director as disclosed in Exhibit 10.5 to AbbVie’s Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q for the quarterly period ended March 31, 2025.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["ABBV"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000110465926116227/0001104659-26-116227-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0002115436-26-000013", "published_at": "2026-10-16T12:02:58Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-16T12:02:58Z", "headline": "Exxon Mobil: Market And Planned Impacts To Earnings", "body": "EX-99.1 2 f8k3q991101626.htm MARKET AND PLANNED IMPACTS TO EARNINGS 1 EXHIBIT 99.1 3Q 2026 Market and Planned Impacts to Earnings The following are selected market and planned factors expected to affect 3Q 2026 results relative to 2Q 2026 results. These factors are limited in scope and generally focus on significant planned maintenance, market dynamics, and seasonal demand patterns. These limited factors are being provided to allow the Company’s subsequent comprehensive earnings release to focus on performance and the impact of management’s strategic decisions. These are current estimates and are not a comprehensive list of all items affecting 3Q results, and actual results may vary, either positively or negatively, from these estimates. It does not include performance-related factors that will contribute to 3Q results, such as operating performance, ongoing improvement initiatives, unscheduled downtime attributable to internal events, or certain other factors. In addition, performance factors may have greater impacts than market and planned factors, negative or positive, on 3Q 2026 results relative to 2Q 2026 results.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["XOM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2115436/000211543626000013/0002115436-26-000013-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000080424-26-000245", "published_at": "2026-10-16T20:25:47Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-16T20:25:47Z", "headline": "Procter & Gamble: Shareholder vote results", "body": "Submission of Matters to a Vote of Security Holders On October 13, 2026, the Company held its 2026 Annual Meeting of Shareholders. Set forth below are the final voting results for each of the proposals submitted to a vote of the shareholders. Proposal 1 – Election of Directors. Each of the following nominees was elected to serve a one-year term on the Company’s Board of Directors. Proposal 2- Ratify Appointment of the Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm. The proposal was approved. Proposal 3 - Advisory Vote to Approve the Company’s Executive Compensation (the “Say on Pay” Vote). The proposal was approved. Proposal 4 - Shareholder Proposal Requesting Lower Threshold for Special Meetings. The proposal was not approved. Proposal 5 - Shareholder Proposal Requesting Policy on Eligibility Thresholds for Proponents of Shareholder Proposals. The proposal was not approved. Proposal 6 - Shareholder Proposal Requesting Annual Reporting on Charitable Contributions. The proposal was not approved. The Company is filing this 8-K pursuant to", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["PG"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/80424/000008042426000245/0000080424-26-000245-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001104659-26-116626", "published_at": "2026-10-16T20:30:20Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-16T20:30:20Z", "headline": "PepsiCo: Other events", "body": "false 0000077476 0000077476 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:Commonstockparvalue123centspershareMember 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointSevenFivePercentNotesDue2027Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointEightSevenFivePercentNotesDue2028Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointFivePercentNotesDue2028Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:FloatingRateNotesDue2028Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ThreePointTwoPercentNotesDue2029Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:OnePointOneTwoFivePercentNotesDue2031Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointFourPercentNotesDue2032Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointSevenFivePercentNotesDue2033Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ThreePointFiveFivePercentNotesDue2034Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ThreePointThreeZeroZeroPercentNotesDue2034Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ThreePointFourFiveZeroPercentNotesDue2037Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ThreePointSevenZeroZeroPercentNotesDue2038Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 pep:ZeroPointEightSevenFiveNotesDue2039Member 2026-10-16 2026-10-16 0000077476 …", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["PEP"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000110465926116626/0001104659-26-116626-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000909832-26-000100", "published_at": "2026-10-16T20:52:57Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-16T20:52:57Z", "headline": "Costco: Director or officer departure or appointment", "body": "Departure of Directors or Certain Officers; Election of Directors; Appointment of Certain Officers; Compensatory Arrangements of Certain Officers. On October 13, 2026, the Compensation Committee of the Board of Directors approved the fiscal 2027 criteria for bonuses to executive officers, with the Nominating and Governance Committee of the Board also approving the environmental and social performance criteria. Executive officers other than the Chief Executive Officer are eligible to receive base bonuses of $400,000. The base amounts include $160,000 based on targets relating to sales and $160,000 based on targets relating to pre-tax income. The potential payment attributable to each goal may be from zero to up to 120% of the target amount, based on the level of achievement. In addition, up to $80,000 can be earned relating to environmental and social objectives based on quantitative performance metrics (including those concerning human capital and environmental-related areas). For fiscal 2027, the Chief Executive Officer is eligible to receive a base bonus of $1.2 million.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["COST"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/909832/000090983226000100/0000909832-26-000100-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-424680", "published_at": "2026-10-19T11:49:23Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-19T11:49:23Z", "headline": "HDFC Bank: Unaudited Consolidated Financial Results For The Quarter And Half Year Ended September 30, 2026", "body": "EX-99 2 d166042dex99.htm EX-99 Exhibit 99 HDFC BANK LIMITED CIN : L65920MH1994PLC080618 Sandoz House, Shivsagar Estate, Dr. Annie Besant Road, Worli, Mumbai 400 018. Website: https://www.hdfc.bank.in, Tel.: 022- 6652 1000, Fax: 022- 2496 0739 UNAUDITED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR THE QUARTER AND HALF YEAR ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2026 Regd. Office : HDFC Bank Ltd., HDFC Bank House, Senapati Bapat Marg, Lower Parel (West), Mumbai - 400013. Consolidated Segment information in accordance with the RBI guidelines and Accounting Standard 17 - Segment Reporting of the operating segments of the Group is as under: *Information about Digital Banking Segment reported as a sub-segment of Retail Banking Segment is related to Digital Banking Units of the Bank. ** Includes the operations of HDFC Life Insurance Company Limited (consolidated) (“HDFC Life”) and HDFC ERGO General Insurance Company Limited (“HDFC Ergo”). *** Segment Results and Liabilities for half year ended September 30, 2025 and year end March 31, 2026 are after considering the impact of floating provisions in the respective segments.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["HDFCBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1144967/000119312526424680/0001193125-26-424680-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-424682", "published_at": "2026-10-19T11:50:39Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-19T11:50:39Z", "headline": "HDFC Bank: Disclosure", "body": "The Board of Directors of the Bank, at its meeting held today, based on the recommendation of the Governance, Nomination and Remuneration Committee (“GNRC”), considered and approved the re-appointment of Mrs. Lily Vadera (DIN: 09400410) as an Independent Director of the Bank for a period of 3 (three) years with effect from November 26, 2026 to November 25, 2029 (both days inclusive), subject to approval of the shareholders of the Bank. We wish to inform you that Mrs. Vadera is not related to any other Directors or Key Managerial Personnel of the Bank. Further, she is not debarred from holding the office of a Director, by virtue of any order passed by SEBI or any other such authority. The aforesaid re-appointment shall be placed before the shareholders of the Bank for their approval, shortly. We further inform that Mr. Kaizad Bharucha (DIN: 02490648), Deputy Managing Director, HDFC Bank has requested cessation from the service of the Bank with effect from the close of business hours on December 31, 2026. The GNRC and the Board of Directors, at their respective meetings held on October 16, 2026 and October 17, 2026, respected the decision of Mr.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["HDFCBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1144967/000119312526424682/0001193125-26-424682-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-425881", "published_at": "2026-10-20T13:16:53Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-20T13:16:53Z", "headline": "Salesforce Signs Definitive Agreement to Acquire Braze", "body": "SAN FRANCISCO & NEW YORK (OCTOBER 20, 2026) — Salesforce (NYSE: CRM), the world’s #1 AI CRM, today announced it has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Braze (NASDAQ: BRZE), a leading customer engagement platform, for approximately $5.66 billion in enterprise value. Under the terms of the agreement, holders of Braze Class A common stock will receive $47.50 in cash per share. Braze helps marketers build deeper customer relationships by responding to customer behavior in real time, coordinating personalized experiences across mobile apps, websites, email, SMS, WhatsApp, and more. Its cloud-native, event-streaming architecture is optimized for high-volume, real-time B2C engagement, continuously updating customer profiles and adapting customer journeys while powering trillions of messages and journey actions each year. BrazeAI extends these capabilities with AI-powered optimization across content, offers, channels, and timing, helping marketers make each interaction more relevant. “Every interaction is an opportunity to wow your customers,” said Patrick Stokes, President, Applications and Marketing, Salesforce.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["CRM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1108524/000119312526425881/0001193125-26-425881-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001065280-26-000290", "published_at": "2026-10-20T20:01:55Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-20T20:01:55Z", "headline": "Netflix: Our summary results, and forecast for Q4, are below.", "body": "__________________________________ 1 Excluding the year over year effect of foreign exchange rate movements and the impact of hedging gains/losses realized as revenues. Assumes foreign exchange rates remained constant with foreign exchange rates from each of the corresponding months of the prior-year period. Q3 Results and Forecast Revenue in Q3 grew 12% year over year (+11% on a foreign exchange (F/X) neutral basis), and was in-line with our forecast. In Q3, revenue growth was driven primarily by subscription revenue, reflecting increases in memberships and pricing, growth in advertising revenue and a favorable impact from F/X rates, net of hedging. Membership growth benefited from continued, healthy retention in every region; globally and in the US, churn improved year-over-year and was better than forecast. Q3’26 operating income totaled $4.5B (+37% year over year) and operating margin of 34.6% was up versus 28.2% in Q3’25. Both Q3 operating income and margin were ahead of forecast due primarily to the timing of expenses and the slight upside in revenue. As a result, diluted EPS for the quarter amounted to $0.87 vs. $0.59 in Q3’25 (+49% year over year).", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["NFLX"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1065280/000106528026000290/0001065280-26-000290-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-426704", "published_at": "2026-10-20T20:15:28Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-20T20:15:28Z", "headline": "JPMorgan Chase: Other events", "body": "JPMORGAN CHASE & CO false 0000019617 0000019617 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 us-gaap:CommonStockMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestinaShareof5.75NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesDDMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestinaShareof6.00NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesEEMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestinaShareof4.75NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesGGMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestInAShareOf455NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesJJMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestInAShareOf4625NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesLLMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:DepositarySharesOneFourHundredthInterestInAShareOf420NonCumulativePreferredStockSeriesMMMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:GuaranteeOfCallableFixedRateNotesDueJune102032OfJPMorganChaseFinancialCompanyLLCMember 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 jpm:GuaranteeOfAlerianMlpIndexETNsDueJanuary282044OfJPMorganChaseFinancialCompanyLlc2Member 2026-10-20 2026-10-20 0000019617 …", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["JPM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000119312526426704/0001193125-26-426704-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-426839", "published_at": "2026-10-20T21:07:52Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-20T21:07:52Z", "headline": "Wipro: Intimation under Regulation 30 of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 - Outcome of Board Meeting", "body": "The Board of Directors (“Board”) of Wipro Limited (“Company”), have at their meeting held over October 14-15, 2026, considered and approved the financial results of the Company for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026, as per Regulation 33 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. Please find enclosed the Audited Standalone and Consolidated financial results under IndAS and Audited Consolidated financial results under IFRS for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026, together with the Auditor’s Report, as approved by the Board today. The financial results are also being made available on the Company’s website at www.wipro.com. The Board Meeting commenced on October 14, 2026 at 4 PM. The Board of Directors finally approved the financial results for the said period at their meeting held on October 15, 2026, which concluded at 3:40 PM.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["WIPRO"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1123799/000119312526426839/0001193125-26-426839-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-426841", "published_at": "2026-10-20T21:08:55Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-20T21:08:55Z", "headline": "Wipro announces results for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026", "body": "IT services segment revenue flat sequentially and increased 0.6% YoY CC Operating Margin at 16.5% expanded 0.5% QoQ EPS increased 4.2% YoY; Operating cash flow at 165.8% of Net income EAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. | BENGALURU, India – October 15, 2026: Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading AI-powered technology services and consulting company, announced financial results under International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) for the quarter ended September 30, 2026. Highlights of the Results Results for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026: Outlook for the Quarter ending December 31, 2026 We expect revenue from our IT Services business segment to be in the range of $2,571 million to $2,625 million*. This translates to sequential guidance of (-)1.5% to (+)0.5% in constant currency terms. 1 Performance for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026 Srini Pallia, CEO and Managing Director, said, “The strategic investments we have been making are beginning to deliver results. They are enhancing our ability to win in new markets, add new clients, and grow existing relationships.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["WIPRO"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1123799/000119312526426841/0001193125-26-426841-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001575872-26-000715", "published_at": "2026-10-21T10:21:02Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-21T10:21:02Z", "headline": "Dr. Reddy's: Dr. Reddy’s Receives DCGI Approval for Zytorvi® (toripalimab) in Advanced Esophageal Squamous Cell Carcinoma, Its Second Approved Indication in India", "body": "” This is for your information and records. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For Dr. Reddy’s Laboratories Limited K Randhir Singh Company Secretary, Compliance Officer & Head-CSR Dr. Reddy’s Receives DCGI Approval for Zytorvi® (toripalimab) in Advanced Esophageal Squamous Cell Carcinoma, Its Second Approved Indication in India The approval expands the use of Zytorvi® beyond its initially approved indication in nasopharyngeal carcinoma (NPC) Hyderabad, India; October 21, 2026: Dr. Reddy's Laboratories Ltd. (BSE: 500124, NSE: DRREDDY, NYSE: RDY, NSEIFSC: DRREDDY; along with its subsidiaries together referred to as “Dr. Reddy’s,”) today announced that the Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation (CDSCO), under the Drugs Controller General of India (DCGI), has approved Zytorvi® (toripalimab) in combination with cisplatin and paclitaxel for the first-line treatment of adult patients with unresectable advanced, recurrent or metastatic esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC).1 Dr. Reddy’s entered into a licensing and commercialization agreement with Junshi Biosciences in 2023 for toripalimab across 21 countries.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["DRREDDY"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1135951/000157587226000715/0001575872-26-000715-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001628280-26-066700", "published_at": "2026-10-21T20:03:35Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-21T20:03:35Z", "headline": "Meta Platforms: Meta Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results", "body": "Announces Establishment of New Class C Common Stock MENLO PARK, Calif. – October 21, 2026 – Meta Platforms, Inc. (Nasdaq: META) today reported financial results for the quarter ended September 30, 2026. \"We hit major milestones this quarter toward delivering personal superintelligence for everyone - including launching Muse and Muse Wonder, our first frontier model,\" said Mark Zuckerberg, Meta founder and CEO. \"Our investments are paying off, the core business is strong, and we're seeing velocity across the board.\" Third Quarter 2026 Financial Highlights Agreement with U.S. State Attorneys General In August 2026, we announced an agreement with 52 attorneys general to resolve litigation related to teen mental health and social media, which provides for payments of up to approximately $18.59 billion. Third quarter 2026 costs and expenses includes a $9.89 billion charge related to this agreement. Excluding this charge, the third quarter 2026: •Income from operations of $12.99 billion would have increased by $9.89 billion to $22.88 billion. •Diluted EPS of $3.83 would have increased by $3.57 to $7.40. •Effective tax rate of 24% would have decreased by 7 percentage points to 17%.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["META"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026066700/0001628280-26-066700-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000051143-26-000093", "published_at": "2026-10-21T20:19:17Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-21T20:19:17Z", "headline": "IBM Releases Third-quarter Results", "body": "EX-99.1 2 ibm-20261021xex991.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 IBM RELEASES THIRD-QUARTER RESULTS Exceeded expectations with accelerated revenue growth led by Software and Infrastructure; Raises outlook for full-year free cash flow ARMONK, N.Y., October 21, 2026 . . . IBM (NYSE: IBM) today announced third-quarter 2026 earnings results. “Disciplined execution throughout the quarter drove accelerated revenue growth and strong free cash flow. Our clients are now deploying Super Intelligence in ways that transform entire operating models, instead of simply addressing narrow or novel problems. IBM's technology and expertise are helping organizations drive growth and serve customers with greater speed, precision and efficiency than ever before,\" said Arvind Krishna, IBM chairman, president and chief executive officer.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["IBM"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/51143/000005114326000093/0000051143-26-000093-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001628280-26-066738", "published_at": "2026-10-21T20:41:42Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-21T20:41:42Z", "headline": "Tesla: Results of operations and financial condition", "body": "Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On October 21, 2026, Tesla, Inc. released its financial results for the quarter ended September 30, 2026 by posting its Third Quarter 2026 Update on its website. The full text of the update is attached hereto as Exhibit 99.1 and is incorporated herein by reference. This information is intended to be furnished under", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["TSLA"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828026066738/0001628280-26-066738-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000070858-26-000494", "published_at": "2026-10-21T21:07:03Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-21T21:07:03Z", "headline": "Bank of America Names Jim Fitterling and Bill Thomas to Board of Directors", "body": "CHARLOTTE, N.C. – The Bank of America Corporation Board of Directors today appointed Jim Fitterling and Bill Thomas as directors, effective immediately. “We are pleased to welcome two seasoned CEOs, who join our Board after leading large, global organizations,” said Brian Moynihan, Chair and Chief Executive Officer, Bank of America. “Jim brings decades of experience in a complex, evolving industry and significant public company board credentials, while Bill brings deep financial expertise in audit, accounting and financial reporting, advising businesses across industries and around the world.” “Jim and Bill are valuable additions to our Board, with complementary leadership experience that will help strengthen our oversight of the company’s long-term strategy,” said Lionel Nowell III, Lead Independent Director, Bank of America. “We have a longstanding, robust succession planning and board refreshment process, which has produced two outstanding leaders to join our Board.” Mr. Fitterling began his career at Dow more than 40 years ago following his graduation from the University of Missouri-Columbia with a bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["BAC"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/70858/000007085826000494/0000070858-26-000494-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0001193125-26-428254", "published_at": "2026-10-22T10:01:09Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T10:01:09Z", "headline": "HDFC Bank: Notice of Postal Ballot", "body": "In compliance with the applicable circulars, the Notice is being sent to all Members whose names appear in the Register of Members / Register of Beneficial Owners maintained by the Depositories viz. National Securities Depository Limited (“NSDL”) and Central Depository Services (India) Limited as on Friday, October 16, 2026 (cut-off date) and whose e-mail addresses are registered with Depository Participants and / or Datamatics Business Solutions Limited, Registrar & Transfer Agents of the Bank. The Bank has engaged the services of NSDL for facilitating remote e-voting to enable the Members to cast their votes electronically. The period for remote e-voting on the resolution set out in the Notice shall commence on Thursday, October 22, 2026 at 10:00 A.M. (IST) and end on Friday, November 20, 2026 at 5:00 P.M. (IST). The Notice is being uploaded on the Bank’s website at https://www.hdfc.bank.in/about-us/corporate-governance/postal-ballot and on the website of NSDL at https://www.evoting.nsdl.com This is for your information and appropriate dissemination. Yours faithfully, For HDFC Bank Limited Sd/- Ajay Agarwal Company Secretary Group Head – Secretarial & Group Oversight", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["HDFCBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1144967/000119312526428254/0001193125-26-428254-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000950103-26-015987", "published_at": "2026-10-22T10:02:58Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T10:02:58Z", "headline": "ICICI Bank: Outcome of Board Meeting held on October 17, 2026", "body": "IBN ICICI Bank Limited (the Bank) Report on Form 6-K In terms of the applicable provisions of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, as amended, (“SEBI Listing Regulations”), we write to inform you that the Board of Directors of ICICI Bank Limited (“the Bank”), at its meeting held today, inter alia, approved the following: We enclose herewith the following as Annexure I: The Board meeting commenced at 9:40 a.m. and concluded at 2:15 p.m. Please take the above information on record.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["ICICIBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1103838/000095010326015987/0000950103-26-015987-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000950103-26-015988", "published_at": "2026-10-22T10:05:17Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T10:05:17Z", "headline": "ICICI Bank: report to the SEC (6-K)", "body": "6-K 1 dp255168_6k.htm FORM 6-K UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 6-K REPORT OF FOREIGN ISSUER PURSUANT TO RULE 13a -16 OR 15d-16 UNDER THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 For the month of October 2026 Commission File Number: 001-15002 ICICI Bank Limited (Translation of registrant’s name into English) ICICI Bank Towers, Bandra-Kurla Complex Mumbai, India 400 051 (Address of principal executive office) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant files or will file annual reports under cover Form 20-F or Form 40-F. Table of Contents Items: OTHER NEWS Subject: Investor Presentation IBN ICICI Bank Limited (the Bank) Report on Form 6-K Please find attached the investor presentation which will be referred during the earnings call with analysts and investors for the financial results of the Bank for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026. The said presentation is being uploaded on the website of the Bank and can be accessed at https://www.icici.bank.in/about-us/qfr This is for your information and records.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["ICICIBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1103838/000095010326015988/0000950103-26-015988-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000950103-26-015989", "published_at": "2026-10-22T10:08:34Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T10:08:34Z", "headline": "ICICI Bank: Disclosure under Indian Listing Regulations", "body": "IBN ICICI Bank Limited (the Bank) Report on Form 6-K Dear Sir/Madam, We wish to inform you that the audio recording of the call with media on the financial results for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026 has been uploaded on the website of the Bank and can be accessed at https://www.icici.bank.in/about-us/news-room Further, the audio recording of earnings call with analysts and investors to discuss the financial results for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2026 has also been uploaded on the website of the Bank and can be accessed at https://www.icici.bank.in/about-us/qfr Please take the above information on record. SIGNATURE Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned, thereunto duly authorised.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["ICICIBANK"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1103838/000095010326015989/0000950103-26-015989-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000080424-26-000250", "published_at": "2026-10-22T11:02:49Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T11:02:49Z", "headline": "Procter & Gamble: Diluted net earnings per share increased by one percent to $1.97. Core earnings per share increased one percent to $2.00 and Currency-neutral Core EPS was unchanged versus the prior year.", "body": "Reported gross margin for the quarter decreased 160 basis points versus the prior year. Core gross margin and currency-neutral Core gross margin for the quarter decreased 150 basis points versus the prior year and excluded the impact from incremental restructuring charges. The decrease was driven by 140 basis points of higher costs from commodities, 140 basis points of product reinvestments, 50 basis points of unfavorable mix and 10 basis points of rounding and other items, partially offset by 120 basis points of gross productivity savings, 50 basis points of tariff impact from lower costs and recognized recoveries and 20 basis points of increased pricing. Reported selling, general and administrative expense (SG&A) as a percentage of sales declined 90 basis points versus year ago. Core SG&A as a percentage of sales decreased 80 basis points versus year ago and decreased 70 basis points on a currency-neutral basis. Core SG&A excluded the impact from incremental restructuring charges.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["PG"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/80424/000008042426000250/0000080424-26-000250-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
{"source": "sec_edgar", "source_event_id": "0000080424-26-000252", "published_at": "2026-10-22T14:29:34Z", "first_seen_at": "2026-10-22T14:29:34Z", "headline": "Procter & Gamble: EARNINGS RELEASE Q1 FY 2027 Results October 22, 2026", "body": "INTEGRATED GROWTH STRATEGY SUPERIORITY TO WIN WITH CONSUMERS PORTFOLIO PERFORMANCE DRIVES BRAND CHOICE ACROSS OUR BUSINESS CONSTRUCTIVE DISRUPTION PRODUCTIVITY TO FUEL INVESTMENTS ORGANIZATION EMPOWERED • AGILE ACCOUNTABLE BUSINESS RESULTS Q1 FY 2027 Continued acceleration on topline despite a challenging macro environment. Expect cost headwinds to increase in next few quarters. Volatility remains. Organic sales grew +4.0% vs prior year. Volume +2.4%, Pricing +0.4%, Mix +1.1%. 10 of 10 product categories and all 6 regions grew organic sales. 29 of our top 50 category/country combinations held or grew share fiscal year to date. Global aggregate value share was in line with the prior year. Core earnings per share were $2.00, +1% vs the prior year. On a currency-neutral basis, core EPS was $1.99, in-line with the prior year. Q1 FY 2027 RESULTS Q1 FY ’27 +4.0%Organic Sales Growth +2.4%Organic Volume Growth +1%Core EPS Growth 0%Currency Neutral Core EPS Growth 93%Free Cash Flow Productivity Q1 FY 2027 RESULTS 1.6% 0.0% 3.5% 0.5% 4.0% Q1 FY '26 Q2 FY '26 Q3 FY '26 Q4 FY '26 Q1 FY '27 Q1 FY 2027 RESULTS Organic Sales Growth • Organic volume +2.4%. • Mix was +1.1%. • Pricing +0.4%.", "language": "en", "provider_symbols": ["PG"], "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/80424/000008042426000252/0000080424-26-000252-index.htm", "source_license": "sec_edgar_public_filing"}
